1
00:00:13,256 --> 00:00:16,705
The model reads the original adapter and proposes a restricted field mapping.

2
00:00:17,469 --> 00:00:19,223
Independent checks accept or reject it.

3
00:00:20,023 --> 00:00:23,430
Failed candidates are retained, and revision attempts have a fixed limit.

4
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:26,366
No model generated Python is executed.

5
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:36,766
Here is the mapping returned by the model, beside eight independent checks.

6
00:00:36,766 --> 00:00:41,200
They cover multiple calls, nested arguments, normal messages, and legacy behavior.

7
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,616
A deliberately corrupted repair must also fail.

8
00:00:43,616 --> 00:00:46,280
The model cannot approve its own work.

9
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:49,375
Now look at the task outcome.

10
00:00:49,375 --> 00:00:53,016
In the real model conversation, local tools return three items

11
00:00:53,016 --> 00:00:54,473
at seven per item.

12
00:00:54,473 --> 00:00:56,520
The original adapter loses the calls.

13
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:58,700
The verified mapping preserves them,

14
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:02,120
and the model returns the independently checked value: twenty-one.

15
00:01:05,202 --> 00:01:09,677
The evidence records the exact model, request count, token usage, and tool results.

16
00:01:10,452 --> 00:01:13,375
These are real API calls with controlled local fixture data.

17
00:01:14,146 --> 00:01:17,599
This is a bounded adapter repair, not a general code sandbox.

